# The reports the monitor writes into this directory are runtime output, so
# they are not tracked.
#
# The directory itself is tracked on purpose. Every compose profile bind
# mounts it into the container, and a bind mount whose source does not exist
# fails to start. Docker creates a missing source for a plain bind mount, but
# it creates it as root, so the container, which runs as uid 1000, could not
# write into it. Tracking the directory keeps it owned by the developer, whose
# uid matches the container's.
*.json
*.csv
*.log
